<title>GREECE: Big Greek banks should be fewer - Alpha Bank boss.</title>
<headline>Big Greek banks should be fewer - Alpha Bank boss.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Alpha Credit Bank, Greece's largest private bank, said the country's four or five biggest commercial banks should become three in a few years.  </p>
<p>&quot;In a few years, these four or five banks with market shares of 4.5 to 39 percent should become three,&quot; Yannis Costopoulos told a news conference.</p>
<p>State National Bank of Greece, state Commercial Bank of Greece, state Ionian bank, private Alpha Credit Bank and private Ergo Bank are the five banks with market shares of 4.49 percent or more, according to figures published on December 31, 1995.</p>
</text>
